FN("PERCENT_RANK", "PERCENT_RANK() OVER (", "PERCENT_RANK() is a window function that returns the relative percent rank of a given row. The following formula is used to calculate the percent rank:", "https://mariadb.com/kb/en/percent_rank/")
FN("PERIOD_ADD", "PERIOD_ADD(P,N)", "Adds N months to period P. P is in the format YYMM or YYYYMM, and is not a date value. If P contains a two-digit year, values from 00 to 69 are converted to from 2000 to 2069, while values from 70 are converted to 1970 upwards.", "https://mariadb.com/kb/en/period_add/")
FN("PERIOD_DIFF", "PERIOD_DIFF(P1,P2)", "Returns the number of months between periods P1 and P2. P1 and P2 can be in the format YYMM or YYYYMM, and are not date values.", "https://mariadb.com/kb/en/period_diff/")
FN("PI", "PI()", "Returns the value of π (pi). The default number of decimal places displayed is six, but MariaDB uses the full double-precision value internally.", "https://mariadb.com/kb/en/pi/")
